[{"location":"#NamedArgs","page":"Home","title":"NamedArgs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for NamedArgs.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"This package allows naming arguments in function calls.","category":"page"},{"location":"#Usage","page":"Home","title":"Usage","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Adding the @na macro in front of a function call allows to use the syntax arg=value also for non-keyword arguments:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"@na my_function(name=\"Federico\", age=35; kw=nothing)","category":"page"},{"location":"#Examples","page":"Home","title":"Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"using NamedArgs\n\nfoo(n::Integer, r::Real; offset=100) = n + r + offset\nfoo(n::Number, c::Char) = \"$(c)_$(n)\"\n\n@na foo(n=42, r=3.14;)\n@na foo(n=42,   3.14;)\n@na foo(  42, r=3.14;)\n@na foo(n=42, r=3.14; offset=200)","category":"page"},{"location":"#Possible-errors","page":"Home","title":"Possible errors","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"@na (1, 2)\n@na foo(n=42, r=3.14)\n@na foo(n=42, \"r\"=3.14;)\n@na foo(n=42, r='x';)","category":"page"},{"location":"#API","page":"Home","title":"API","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"#NamedArgs.@na-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Home","title":"NamedArgs.@na","text":"@na f(arg=val, ...; kwargs)\n\nAllow naming arguments in a function call.\n\nSee the module documentation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"}]
